---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---


<BaseLayout title="PLC Conveyor Control · Ngwashi Anthony" active="projects">
  <main data-screen-label="Project detail">
    <div class="wrap crumb"><a href="/projects">← Projects</a></div>

    <section class="wrap proj-head">
      <div>
        <span class="kicker">PROJ-03 · Control · PLC · 2025</span>
        <h1 class="h-xl">PLC Conveyor Control</h1>
        <p class="lede">A simple conveyor system programmed in OpenPLC that detects boxes with a sensor and pushes them from one conveyor to another using a pneumatic pusher.</p>
        <div class="tags" style="margin-top:24px;">
          <span class="tag tag-accent">Control</span><span class="tag">PLC</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="head-meta">
        <div class="meta-row"><span class="k">Type</span><span class="v">Academic project</span></div>
        <div class="meta-row"><span class="k">PLC</span><span class="v">OpenPLC</span></div>
        <div class="meta-row"><span class="k">Status</span><span class="v accent">Complete</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="frame hero-frame">
        <img src="/images/plc-editor-overview.png" alt="OpenPLC editor showing the conveyor control program" class="expandable" />
        <span class="frame-corner tl"></span><span class="frame-corner tr"></span>
        <span class="frame-corner bl"></span><span class="frame-corner br"></span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="body-grid">
        <article class="writeup">
          <h2>The idea</h2>
          <p>This project introduced me to PLC programming using OpenPLC, an open-source platform for programmable logic controllers. The task was straightforward: build a program that moves boxes from one conveyor belt to another using a sensor to detect when a box is in position and a pusher to shove it across.</p>
          <p class="mono-note">// goal: detect a box, push it to the next conveyor, repeat.</p>

          <h2>How it works</h2>
          <p>The system has two conveyors running side by side. When a box arrives on the first conveyor, a sensor detects its presence. Once the box is in the right position, the PLC triggers a pneumatic pusher that slides the box sideways onto the second conveyor. After the pusher extends and retracts, the system waits for the next box.</p>
          <p>The entire logic is written in ladder diagram (LD) within the OpenPLC editor. It reads the sensor input, controls the pusher output, and uses timers to manage the push and retract cycle. Simple, but it covers the core concepts: inputs, outputs, timing, and sequential control.</p>

          <div class="photo-pair">
            <div>
              <div class="frame"><img src="/images/plc-ladder-logic.png" alt="Ladder logic diagram for the conveyor pusher control" class="expandable" /></div>
              <div class="photo-cap">FIG 1: Ladder logic program controlling the sensor and pusher</div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="frame"><img src="/images/plc-factory-io.png" alt="Conveyor system with boxes being pushed between belts" class="expandable" /></div>
              <div class="photo-cap">FIG 2: The conveyor setup with sensor and pusher mechanism</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h2>Program structure</h2>
          <p>The ladder logic is split into two main rungs. The first rung reads the sensor input and sets a flag when a box is detected in position. The second rung uses that flag to trigger the pusher, with a timer controlling how long the pusher stays extended before retracting. A second timer ensures the pusher is fully retracted before the system accepts the next box.</p>
          <p>OpenPLC made this easy to prototype. The editor compiles the ladder diagram to run on standard hardware, so I could test the logic without needing a physical PLC unit. The simulation showed the sensor triggering, the pusher firing, and the box moving to the second conveyor in real time.</p>

          <div class="photo-single">
            <div class="frame">
              <img src="/images/plc-factory-io.gif" alt="Animation of boxes being pushed from one conveyor to another" class="expandable" />
              <span class="frame-corner tl"></span><span class="frame-corner tr"></span><span class="frame-corner bl"></span><span class="frame-corner br"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="photo-cap">FIG 3: Simulation showing the full sensor-push-reset cycle in action</div>
          </div>

          <h2>What I learned</h2>
          <p>This project was my first real exposure to PLC programming. Before this, I only knew about microcontrollers like Arduino. A PLC works differently: it scans inputs, executes the ladder logic, updates outputs, and repeats, cycle after cycle. Understanding that scan cycle, and how timers and flags work in ladder logic, was the key takeaway. It is a different way of thinking about control compared to writing code in C or Python.</p>
        </article>

        <aside>
          <div class="specs">
            <div class="specs-head"><span class="t">Specifications</span><span class="mono mono-accent">v1</span></div>
            <div class="spec-group">
              <div class="g-label">Controller</div>
              <div class="spec-line"><span class="sk">Platform</span><span class="sv">OpenPLC</span></div>
              <div class="spec-line"><span class="sk">Language</span><span class="sv">Ladder Diagram (LD)</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="spec-group">
              <div class="g-label">Hardware</div>
              <div class="spec-line"><span class="sk">Input</span><span class="sv">1x sensor (box detect)</span></div>
              <div class="spec-line"><span class="sk">Output</span><span class="sv">1x pusher (pneumatic)</span></div>
              <div class="spec-line"><span class="sk">Conveyors</span><span class="sv">2 (source + destination)</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="spec-group">
              <div class="g-label">Logic</div>
              <div class="spec-line"><span class="sk">Detection</span><span class="sv">Sensor on conveyor 1</span></div>
              <div class="spec-line"><span class="sk">Action</span><span class="sv">Pusher extends, retracts</span></div>
              <div class="spec-line"><span class="sk">Timing</span><span class="sv">Timer-controlled cycle</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </aside>
      </div>

      <div class="nextprev">
        <a class="txtlink" href="/projects/voltage-regulator"><span class="arrow">←</span> Voltage Regulator</a>
        <a class="txtlink" href="/projects/auralink">Auralink <span class="arrow">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="lightbox" class="lightbox">
      <img id="lightbox-img" src="" alt="" />
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .crumb { padding-block: 28px 0; }
  .crumb a { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3); }
  .crumb a:hover { color: var(--accent); }

  .proj-head { padding-block: 26px 34px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.6fr 1fr; gap: 48px; align-items: end; }
  .proj-head h1 { margin: 16px 0 0; }
  .proj-head .lede { margin-top: 20px; max-width: 40ch; }
  .head-meta { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0; }
  .meta-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; padding: 11px 0; border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--line-2); }
  .meta-row:first-child { border-top: 1px dashed var(--line-2); }
  .meta-row .k { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-3); }
  .meta-row .v { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 500; }

  .frame { position: relative; overflow: hidden; background: var(--paper-2); }
  .frame img { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: contain; }
  .frame img.expandable { cursor: zoom-in; transition: opacity 0.15s ease; }
  .frame img.expandable:hover { opacity: 0.85; }

  .hero-frame { aspect-ratio: 21 / 9; }

  .body-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 320px; gap: 56px; padding: 56px 0 0; align-items: start; }
  .writeup h2 { margin: 42px 0 14px; font-size: 28px; }
  .writeup h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .writeup p { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .writeup .mono-note { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-3); border-left: 2px solid var(--accent); padding: 4px 0 4px 16px; margin: 22px 0; line-height: 1.6; }

  .photo-pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; margin: 28px 0; }
  .photo-pair .frame { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; }
  .photo-cap { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: var(--ink-3); margin-top: 8px; }
  .photo-single { margin: 28px 0; }
  .photo-single .frame { aspect-ratio: 16 / 8; }

  .specs { position: sticky; top: calc(var(--nav-h) + 20px); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 5px; background: var(--paper); overflow: hidden; }
  .specs-head { padding: 16px 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; background: var(--paper-2); }
  .specs-head .t { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .spec-group { padding: 16px 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .spec-group:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .spec-group .g-label { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .spec-line { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; padding: 5px 0; font-size: 14px; }
  .spec-line .sk { color: var(--ink-3); }
  .spec-line .sv { color: var(--ink); text-align: right; font-weight: 500; }

  .nextprev { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 24px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); margin-top: 64px; padding: 28px 0; }

  .lightbox {
    display: none;
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.88);
    z-index: 1000;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 40px;
    cursor: zoom-out;
  }
  .lightbox.open { display: flex; }
  .lightbox img {
    max-width: 100%;
    max-height: 100%;
    object-fit: contain;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .proj-head { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; align-items: start; }
    .body-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 40px; }
    .specs { position: static; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .photo-pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>

<script>
  const lightbox = document.getElementById("lightbox");
  const lightboxImg = document.getElementById("lightbox-img") as HTMLImageElement;

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLImageElement>("img.expandable").forEach((img) => {
    img.addEventListener("click", () => {
      lightboxImg.src = img.src;
      lightboxImg.alt = img.alt;
      lightbox?.classList.add("open");
    });
  });

  lightbox?.addEventListener("click", () => {
    lightbox.classList.remove("open");
  });

  document.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
    if (e.key === "Escape") lightbox?.classList.remove("open");
  });
</script>
